<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Palio of Asti</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1275</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Palio of Asti is a bareback horse race held each September in Asti, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/piedmont">Piedmont</a>, first recorded in 1275, when the Astigiani ran it under the walls of Alba during a war. Riders represent the city's districts and nearby towns, and the race is preceded by a large historical procession in medieval costume. It is one of the oldest such races in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/palio-of-asti.jpg" alt="Palio of Asti" width="320" height="250" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Original uploader was Faberh at it.wikipedia · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Part_corsa_del_palio_di_asti_XVIII_secolo.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
